# LF in the repository, whatever the working tree uses.
#
# This exists because a diff was made unreadable without anyone choosing to make it unreadable.
# 173 of this repository's 175 tracked text blobs already store LF and two stored CRLF, so LF was
# already the convention and nothing declared it. An edit to one of the two anomalies normalised it
# on the way past, and the diff for that file came back 1248 insertions and 1018 deletions instead
# of the 292 and 62 that were real, which hid the change inside its own whitespace.
#
# The mechanism, worth knowing before writing another edit script: Path.read_text() decodes with
# universal newlines, so a CRLF file arrives as LF and any "preserve what was there" logic that
# inspects the decoded string sees LF and preserves that. Reading with newline="" is what actually
# preserves them. Declaring the convention here means it no longer matters which one a script does.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Built assets: whatever the bundler emitted, byte for byte.
frontend/dist/** -text
